.page-header
  .container
    .eyebrow // documentation
    %h1 The manuals.
    %p
      Reference documentation for MVC::Keayl and the modules built around it.

.container
  %ul.doc-set-grid
    %li.doc-set
      %h2
        %a{href: '/docs/MVC-Keayl'} MVC::Keayl
      %p
        The framework itself: the request and response objects, middleware and
        server adapters, routing, controllers and views, sessions and security,
        caching and streaming, background jobs and mail, and the command-line
        tool that generates it all.
      %p.doc-set-meta 37 pages
    %li.doc-set
      %h2
        %a{href: '/docs/MVC-Keayl-Admin'} MVC::Keayl::Admin
      %p
        An administration interface generated from your models: registering
        resources, index pages with filters and scopes, show pages and forms,
        custom actions, navigation, and authorization.
      %p.doc-set-meta 21 pages
    %li.doc-set
      %h2
        %a{href: '/docs/ORM-ActiveRecord'} ORM::ActiveRecord
      %p
        The object-relational mapper: migrations and generators, finders and
        relations, joins and aggregation, persistence and callbacks,
        validations, transactions, and encryption.
      %p.doc-set-meta 44 pages
    %li.doc-set
      %h2
        %a{href: '/docs/Template-HAML'} Template::HAML
      %p
        The template language the views are written in: tags and attributes,
        indentation and whitespace, embedded code and control flow, filters,
        layouts and partials, helpers, and the plugin API.
      %p.doc-set-meta 22 pages
